        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>Late October - Agnarr Slain.</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									EoD up until this point had killed all pre-EP bosses accept for Rallos Zek, Sol Ro and Agnarr.  Agnarr was slain 28th October to 50ish Clan Dread members in a flawless end fight.  The only thing stopping us getting into the Plane of Air, Earth and Water is now Rallos Zek.<BR><BR>
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000920.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000920.JPG" width=537 height=446 id=i3></a><BR>
										
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>Early November - Rallos Zek Slain - EOD enters Elemental Planes!</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									After around ten or so tries at the script and around 5 of them being on the final real Rallos Zek in the arena Clan Dread finally is victorious!   When we first started to try the script in October it was still in a bugged state.  Bugged in that Vallon Zek assisted Tallon.  Indeed that didn't stop us.  In fact we managed to kill both Vallon and Tallon at the same time.  We split our raid force in two - 30 going to kill Tallon and the other 25 or so on Vallon.  We killed them both within a few seconds of each other - spawned the fake - slain him like a PoV desert trash mob and headed to the arena.  Unfortunately our experience of the final arena battle was not so great.  Like all guilds there is a large learning curve on the Rallos Zek script.  Each time you do it - you perfect the old fights and learn the new ones.  In between our arena battles Sony finally fixed the problem.  Sure enough it meant we could do he VZ/TZ part even faster but that never really changed the final encounter.<BR><BR>On 1st November Rallos Zek was taken down!  Most of the raid even managed to get out alive.  Out of 66 people on the raid 63 were flagged.  Only 3 (piggies) missed the flag - again due to silly Sony bugs with piggie invites.<BR><BR>Clan Dread were now Elemental Flagged.  We had been doing the Tower of Solusek Ro minis for a couple of weeks now and we had seen Sol Ro himself up and unchallenged many times - all the time wishing to get access to unload the mack.  Now we would have our chance on Sol Ro.  We weren't happy with just Plane of Air, Earth or Water access - we want full access and right away!<BR><BR>Indeed that night right after RZ 23 Clan Dread zoned into the Tower and up the portal to Sol Ro's lair.   We engaged Sol Ro for the first time and with a minimum break of 23 people we got Solusek Ro to 20%.  Not bad for a first try and with so few people.  We failed on Sol Ro but we were laughing.  Laughing because we knew the next raid he would fall - and fall fast n hard.  Solusek Ro was an easy mob - especially after what we just accomplished with Rallos Zek.<BR><BR>The focus now would be get more Dread flagged for the lair and challenge him once again.  Plane of Fire was awaiting us...<BR><BR>
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000921.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000921.JPG" width=296 height=146 id=i4></a><BR>
										
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000922.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000922.JPG" width=413 height=292 id=i5></a><BR>
										
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>Early November (the next day) - Solusek Ro Slain!  EoD gains access to Pla</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									2nd November Solusek Ro was slain to Clan Dread.  We had a fair few people with us.  Unfortunately we didn't have that many flagged for lair so we killed a few minis to complete more flags.  We then entered the tower and in a flawless raid killed Sol Ro.  <BR><BR>Clan Dread were now a fully elemental planes guild.  All the hard work of back flagging - wiping on mobs like Rallos Zek and the Agnarr script and finally paid off.  We hailed the PP and took a lava dip to zone directly into Fire..!<BR><BR>Fennin Ro should be quaking in his boots...<BR><BR>
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000923.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000923.JPG" width=478 height=443 id=i6></a><BR>
										
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>Early November - Back flagging</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									Now that we had 30 or so EP flagged 2/3rds of the guild still needed one flag here and one flag there.  The PoP flags were indeed fragmented.  EoD is not a 24/7 raid guild.  We are hardcore weekend warriors.  We don't boot people for not attending our Fri/Sat raids but then when people are on we raid them hard.  Hard enough to get into the Elementals!  The downside of this is that you can quickly end up with flag fragmentation across the guild where 60% of members need only one flag and only an average of 3-4 members needing the same flag.  This means you have to do 'Dreaded back flagging'.  We wouldn't back flag forever though - after all we have a date with the Plane of Time and a tight schedule to keep.  <BR><BR>In the 2nd week of November we killed Rallos Zek (2nd time - only 5 days later), Solusek Ro Minis, Rydda'Dar, HoH Villager & Nomad Trials, Agnarr, Mithaniel Marr, Solusek Ro, Saryn, KoS, Vallon Zek and...Solusek Ro again.  That was two very busy weekends (about five raid days).<BR><BR>..and that my friends is it for now - the 2nd back flagging extravaganza was complete.  Now time to farm some elemental gear..<BR><BR>
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000924.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000924.JPG" width=529 height=282 id=i7></a><BR>
										
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000925.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000925.JPG" width=395 height=267 id=i8></a><BR>
										
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>Mid November - Plane of Fire - First Raid - Mass Mini Mackage!</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									On a Friday night we did General Druav, Jaxolix (fire bird), Craire (fire bird), Qua (fire bird), Blazzax, Pyronis, Babnoxis. ALL SLAIN in one night - guild firsts.  We did wipe twice during the night - and both of those were to not being fully prepared for certain mobs AEs.  We got our shit together however and unloaded the mack.  I'd say 2 wipes to 7 PoF minis isn't bad - given it was our first try and with around 50 people.  Sure enough we would improve on this!<BR><BR>The next day (Sat) we returned to PoF to do General Reparm and Arch Mage Yozanni.  We then went to Plane of Earth and engaged our first big PoE mob - Tantisala Jaggedtooth - the HUGE crocodile at the temple.  Needless to say we was flawlessly taken down.  There was no stopping us now - now we were on a roll.<BR><BR>
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000926.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000926.JPG" width=375 height=232 id=i9></a><BR>
										
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000927.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000927.JPG" width=367 height=186 id=i10></a><BR>
										
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>Mid November - Plane of Fire - Fennin Ro Script</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									It was a Friday night - our main raid.  Fennin RO's trigger - the Guardian of Doomfire was up.  We decided the raid would be on Fennin.  We took our Guardian within a blink of an eye and marched 50 or so Clan Dread through the gates and up towards the first script minis.<BR><BR>Mini after mini fell flawlessly.  We were certainly used to the bashing and knew exactly how to deal with it.  We killed all the minis and moved in closer for Fennin.  It was our first time meeting him and we spent a little time trying things out.  In typical EoD style we don't just take someone's thoughts or advice on a mob - we try everything - test everything - event new styles and new strategies to take down a mob.  <BR><BR>This night however belonged to Fennin.  Sure enough we could get to him but our strategy needed refining.  It was getting late and we vowed to return for him.<BR><BR>The next day we returned to PoF.  Unfortunately Fennin and his script was down but popping like rabbits in a field were all of the minis.  We killed Druav, three fire birds, Magmaton, Babnoxis, Blaz, Pyronis, Reparm and the Arch Mage.  Basically we killed EVERYHING in the zone which didn't have an 'a ' at the start.  We did it all within around five hours too.  Our numbers? Around 42.  Our proud moment was the kill of General Reparm the 3k quadding 2k wtf procing bad ass (generally accepted to be the hardest mob in the PoF) with 42 - a totally flawless fight.  Indeed we are now looking at how to improve our kills with lower numbers.  Ideally reaching a position of around 18-24 for most mobs.  Some mobs we can already do with this figure.<BR><BR>
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000931.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000931.JPG" width=534 height=413 id=i11></a><BR>
										
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000929.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000929.JPG" width=383 height=183 id=i12></a><BR>
										
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>Late November- Plane of Air - Avatars 'blown' away!</b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									During our PoF farming we have been hitting up Air too.  We have conquered three Avatars in Air atm - Wind, Smoke and Mist.  They died very easily and their minis to trigger them were exceptionally easy.  We are now up to Dust and learning the trigger script.  We don't expect to be hanging around on this too long and right after Dust falls - it's a case of: Hello Xegony!<BR><BR>Now that Fennin is down we will continue to hit Fire but focus on Air and then start to learn Water.  We are 1/5th of the way to Time and we don't intend to slow down!<BR><BR>
										<a href="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000930.JPG" target="popimg"><img src="http://pdm-works.mmaweb.net/WebMain/UniImgDir/Guild_1/gsite/UI00000930.JPG" width=537 height=325 id=i13></a><BR>
										
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							<center><img src="images/sword_9868.GIF"></center><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
    		            <tr>
        		            <td valign=top>
							
									<font color=white size=5><b>Current News - December </b></font><BR>
		                    	    <BR>
									<font color=white>
									We have 65 Clan Drad flagged for EP and we are capable of taking down Fennin with 50 - but probably reducing this to 30.  We estimate to take out Xegony with 40-50 and again reduce that number.  We will then be actively attemping COirnav.  When Coirn is down (or during times which Coirn is not available) we will be doing the Plane of Earth rings.<BR><BR>We would like to recruit more EP flagged people.  We are particularly looking for Clerics, Druids and Shaman - but all classes are welcome.  We look for skilled people rather than mindless players of a class.  In EoD our 'minimum break' ideals will test your metal to the max.  If you are looking to get into Time and then progress from the bottom up through GoD and Omens then perhaps we are the guild for you.<BR><BR>If you want to be part of this progression and you have something to offer - hit the Apply  on the left.<BR><BR>Maj<BR><BR>
      	              </td>
	                </tr>
	                
